228	    /** A claim's due now: a settled claim's frozen due; else the greater of the sheet's floor in force on the
229	     *  claim's date and its figure (the one its last statement bound it to, else its live rate figure) plus, while it
230	     *  is overdue (OPEN or PENDING and its due-by — fixed when it was created — plus its grade's grace days before the
231	     *  sheet's today), for every full 30 days it is overdue, the sheet's late percent in force on that boundary date (the
232	     *  due-by plus the grace plus 30, 60,
233	     *  90 ... days) of that figure plus the charges of the boundaries before it (compounding), each rounded to two decimals by the claim's rounding, the charges added up (a
234	     *  boundary whose percent is 0.00 adds nothing). A statement never binds the charge: it keeps following the
235	     *  sheet's today until settling freezes it in. A correction (a negative amount) has no floor and no late charge,
236	     *  nor does a deferred claim have a charge (it is not overdue). Null when it has no figure. */
237	    public BigDecimal dueNow(String sheetId, Claim claim) {
238	        if (claim.due() != null) return new BigDecimal(claim.due());
239	        BigDecimal figure = figure(sheetId, claim);
240	        if (figure == null || new BigDecimal(claim.amount()).signum() < 0) return figure;
241	        BigDecimal due = figure.add(lateCharge(sheetId, claim, figure));
242	        return due.max(settings.floor(sheetId, LocalDate.parse(claim.date())));
243	    }
